  "id": "Compound::DB01200 - Gene::3358",
  "verbalization": "Bromocriptine, a member of the ergoline class, is implicated in the relationship with Htr2c through multiple mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Bromocriptine, through its inclusion in Ergolines, binds to Htr2c via interactions with Cabergoline, a closely related ergoline compound. This binding is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) relationship between Bromocriptine and Cabergoline, which points to a shared biological category—Nitrogen Molecular Entity and Dopamine Agonist—indicating a common biochemical role. The presence of Htr2c as a target in both Bromocriptine and Cabergoline pathways underscores a potential mechanism involving receptor binding or signaling pathways. The integrated evidence suggests that Bromocriptine may exert its effects through a shared mode of action with Cabergoline, targeting Htr2c via a common biochemical pathway, thereby supporting a direct relationship between Bromocriptine and Htr2c.",
